    "Prop 4.9 is done by the English support-profile obstruction (CompactPlacement.lean). Statement changes: [CategoricalUnbounded K], ℵ₀ ≤ σ, natural-parameter clause hnat, coherence clause hcoh; the prescription for p is the diagram of a tuple q p of E(I), so possibility needs no hypothesis. Hard edge proposition_4_2 → proposition_4_9 added (strong-map clause of Prop 4.2). Lemma 4.10 is unblocked: its only hard dep is Prop 4.9; a natural instantiation of q p is via a strong map B → E(I) fixing p (Prop 4.2 at μ), which satisfies hnat and hcoh.",
    "Lemma 4.10 is done (BoundedDiagramLift.lean, PlacedTesting.lean). Statement changes: the old statement was vacuous, since each test clause carried D.t μ ≤ Model.card B while Model.card B = μ < D.t μ (StableDiagram.above). Now the lift clauses are at the bounded levels ρ < μ (the diagrams D(d, X; B), |X| < μ, whose thresholds lie below μ), J is produced with D.t μ ≤ ‖E(J)‖, and uniqueness is the level-μ comparison over all of A; added [CategoricalUnbounded K], hcat : Categorical K μ, ℵ₀ ≤ σ, and hg : PlacedTester K E D g. PlacedTester is the English Prop 4.8 over the base (placements of a σ-tuple over E(I) that differ over A differ over ≤ g(σ) positions of I); it is proved as proposition_4_8_over_base / exists_placedTester from Lemma 4.7 (type_u_witness_set) by the frozen-data / ordinal-vector argument, because proposition_4_8 on the support encoding only tests two full lists on their own joint support. So lemma_4_7 → proposition_4_8 is hard again, and proposition_4_8, proposition_4_2 (strong maps B → E(I) fixing parameters), proposition_4_3 (common hulls, categoricity at μ) → lemma_4_10 are hard.",
    "Thm 4.11 is done (ClosedLevels.lean, ClosedLevelAmalgam.lean, ClosedLevelTypes.lean); Section 4 is complete (no sorry in AEC/Section4), and Prop 5.6 is unblocked. S = closure points μ > ℓ of {t, g}. Statement changes: added [CategoricalUnbounded K], E : OrderPresentation K, hg : PlacedTester K E D g (replacing the monotone-only g). Clause 2: added ℵ₀ ≤ σ; the old right side was vacuous (tests at level μ under D.t μ ≤ Model.card Bᵢ = μ < D.t μ); it is now the tests at the bounded levels ρ < μ (as in lemma_4_10) over all parameter lists p : β → A with #β ≤ g σ + ls K. β is quantified inside the iff, since for one fixed β the iff fails when β is small; the bound is g σ + ls K because PlacedTester bounds positions of I and ≤ g(σ) positions support ≤ g(σ) + ℓ elements of A. Clause 3: the old form compared x, y ∈ A under g₀ = g₁ on A, which forces x = y and holds for any injection A → μ; it is now a code for the elements of all μ-extensions (B, f) of A, with code B₀ f₀ x = code B₁ f₁ y iff an amalgam over A identifies x with y (the old form is the case B₀ = B₁ = A). Hard edges proposition_4_2 → theorem_4_11 (strong-map clause, StableDiagram.to_strong) and proposition_4_8 → theorem_4_11 (placed tester) added."
