      "detail": "ClosedLevels.lean: closure points of {t, g} above any κ (exists_closurePoint_ge, an ω-tower of successors of 2^θ ⊔ sup of t, g below θ; no monotonicity of g needed), categoricity by Prop 4.3 (categorical_of_closurePoint), unions of countable strong chains (exists_strong_of_nat_exhaustion), transport of a tuple with a level-μ diagram into a fixed categorical model (StableDiagram.exists_transport). ClosedLevelAmalgam.lean: A ≅ E(I), I of order type μ; G = E(J) of a categoricity size ≥ t(μ) (exists_categorical_extension); LiftsTuple = a tuple of E(J) lifting the bounded diagrams over A; one step exists_lift_extension (Lemma 4.10 lift of the longer tuple, uniqueness at level μ over all of A against the given lift, transport into G); countable tower of strong submodels smaller than μ (exists_strong_tower, countable cofinality); each lifted stage is a strong map by D.to_strong in a common hull (exists_strong_of_liftsTuple); the union is a strong map B → G over A extending a prescribed lift (exists_strong_embedding_over); amalgams exists_amalgam_of_common_lift / exists_amalgam_of_agreeOn (LS hull of size μ in G); sufficiency of the tests by the placed tester (agreeOn_univ_of_tests), necessity by D.of_strong (StableDiagram.same_of_amalgam). ClosedLevelTypes.lean: ClosedLevel.amalgamation, ClosedLevel.tuple_amalgamation_iff, ClosedLevel.singleton_types; a singleton placement is coded by its label and the cuts of its finite support in I (Placement.singletonCode, ≤ μ codes mk_singletonCode_le, equal codes give the same comparison over A by sameNaturalDiagram_of_pattern), code of an element = least code of a placement lifting it. Statement changes: [CategoricalUnbounded K], E, hg : PlacedTester K E D g; clause 2 with ℵ₀ ≤ σ and bounded-level tests ρ < μ over all parameter lists of length ≤ g σ + ls K (β inside the iff); clause 3 generalized from the degenerate x, y ∈ A form to elements of all μ-extensions of A. No sorry (axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound)."
    },
